Kimi-K3.1 mLite (impl=vllm) on ROCm: kernel backend selection (MLITE_K31_BACKEND=rocm), ROCm GEMM / MXFP4 dequant /
MoE alignment kernels and VJPs, and the batch-invariant paths that mirror the rollout under VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1:
dense BI GEMMs and LoRA epilogue, virtual TP (MLITE_K31_BI_VTP) reproducing a TP=N rollout's partial sums, BI KDA
(k31kdabi plugin), BI MXFP4 MoE with expert LoRA (k31lora.bi_moe), and the rollout's pinned AttnRes tiling.
Why BI needs it: the trainer forward must run the same kernels, tiles and reduction order as the BI rollout.
Upstream status: not yet proposed.

